cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or method, please cite the manuscript below."
title: "module-aging-toolkit: a single-cell framework with built-in controls for module- and cell-type-resolved transcriptomic clocks"
abstract: >-
  Code, result tables, figures and verification script for the manuscript "Opening the composite clock:
  a single-cell framework with built-in controls for mortality-associated module signatures, demonstrated
  in pulmonary fibrosis". Version 0.2.0 corresponds to the revised manuscript (scripts/revision,
  results/revision, figures_revision, supplementary_revision); version 0.1.0 corresponds to the original
  submission. The toolkit's own code is MIT-licensed; third_party/tage_prep.py and Supplementary Tables
  S3a-b are derived from Materials distributed under the MGB Open Access License 1.0 and are restricted to
  non-commercial academic use (see THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md).
